# Secrets and private context — never committed
private/
*.env
.env*

# …except the scaffolding template's private/, which is the file that DOCUMENTS the rule
# above. templates/project/private/README.md matches the bare `private/` and was tracked only
# because it predates that rule — grandfathered, not intended. The same shape, unstated, cost
# @nytka/cli 0.4.0 the file: in kd-nytka the vendored copy of this template was newer than the
# ignore rule, so it was never tracked, never checked out on CI, and never packed.
#
# The negation names the DIRECTORY, not the file in it: git never descends into an excluded
# directory, so `!.../private/README.md` on its own re-includes nothing. Verified with
# `git check-ignore -v --no-index`. `**/` so the same line holds in kd-nytka, where the
# vendored template sits under packages/cli/.
!**/templates/project/private/

# Transient files the safe writer makes — the lock it holds while replacing a file, and the
# temp file it renames over the target. Both live for milliseconds; they are listed so a
# `git add -A` that races a write cannot commit one. Dot-prefixed patterns on purpose:
# a bare `*.lock` would also swallow a real yarn.lock or Cargo.lock.
.*.lock
.*.tmp

node_modules/
.DS_Store
